    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "You mentioned that strict enforcement can disrupt supply chains. But if we look at it from a sovereignty standpoint, isn't a lack of control over who is entering the country fundamentally a failure of the state to maintain its own borders? It seems like a pretty clear-cut issue for national security.",
